ble by \\(9\\). So, \\(54\\) is a lucky integer.\n   - For \\(63\\): The sum of the digits is \\(6 + 3 = 9\\), and \\(63\\) is divisible by \\(9\\). So, \\(63\\) is a lucky integer.\n   - For \\(72\\): The sum of the digits is \\(7 + 2 = 9\\), and \\(72\\) is divisible by \\(9\\). So, \\(72\\) is a lucky integer.\n   - For \\(81\\): The sum of the digits is \\(8 + 1 = 9\\), and \\(81\\) is divisible by \\(9\\). So, \\(81\\) is a lucky integer.\n   - For \\(90\\): The sum of the digits is \\(9 + 0 = 9\\), and \\(90\\) is divisible by \\(9\\). So, \\(90\\) is a lucky integer.\n   - For \\(99\\): The sum of the digits is \\(9 + 9 = 18\\), and \\(99\\) is not divisible by \\(18\\) but is divisible by \\(9\\). So, \\(99\\) is not a lucky integer because it must be divisible by the correct sum of its digits.\n\nThus, the least positive multiple of 9 that is not a lucky integer is \\(\\boxed{99}\\).",
